# Single page app fallback. React Router owns the routes, so a cold load or a
# refresh on /board/tnt-2026-10-02 must serve index.html rather than 404.
#
# The 200 matters: it rewrites without changing the URL, so the router still
# sees the real path. A 301 or 302 would send the browser back to /.
#
# Cloudflare's build system sometimes flags this rule as an infinite loop and
# silently ignores it. If deep links 404 after a deploy, that is the cause, and
# the fallback is a Workers Static Assets deploy with
# "not_found_handling": "single-page-application".
